  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR splits `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs` (1685 lines) along the domain seams. It is a mechanical move. The code of each function is the same. No widget, label, role, order, id or command changes.\n\n`panes.rs` keeps the keyboard layer (`shortcuts`), `TYPES` and the browser re-exports. It re-exports the old names, so each caller keeps its `panes::` path. No user file changes. The re-exports that only tests use have `#[cfg(test)]`.\n\nNew files in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes/`:\n\n| File | Lines | Holds |\n|---|---|---|\n| `panes.rs` | 153 | keyboard layer, `TYPES`, module list, re-exports |\n| `panes/cmd.rs` | 325 | `Cmd`, the group plan, `ribbon_plan`, labels, `text_of`, `tip_of` |\n| `panes/gates.rs` | 305 | `enabled`, the Create gates and routes, `toggled`, `icon_of` |\n| `panes/run.rs` | 135 | `run_cmd`, `toggle_pin` |\n| `panes/ribbon_layout.rs` | 228 | `Cell`, `Drop`, `ribbon_cells`, `machine_rows`, `view_rows_of` |\n| `panes/mode_tabs.rs` | 201 | the machine-mode tabs and the machine door dropdown |\n| `panes/section_drop.rs` | 178 | the section door dropdown |\n| `panes/ribbon_strip.rs` | 200 | `ribbon`: the strip, cells, captions, other doors, build badge |\n| `panes/status_bar.rs` | 104 | `status`: the status strip |\n\nTwo blocks of the old `ribbon` function became functions, because `ribbon` alone had 423 lines: `section_drop` and `machine_drop`. Each block moved as it was. `ribbon` calls them at the same point and in the same order, with the same `egui::Id` base.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `crates/ui` `#[test]` count: 1964 before, 1964 after. No test file changes.\n- Shell render, dark and light (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light` with `UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1`), on the same machine (winbuild, WARP software adapter): the PNGs of the merge base `d38fd5421` and of this head `323c70618` are byte-identical (SHA-256 `b241ca38...` dark, `0db11e13...` light).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe two images are byte-identical (same SHA-256).\n\nBefore (merge base `d38fd5421`):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4398/before.png)\n\nAfter (this head `323c70618`):\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4398/after.png)\n\n## Tests (head `323c70618`, lane winbuild)\n\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. Steps: ui build, ui lib (unit tests), `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `contour_dxf_sketch`, `sinker_setup`, `tap_hand`, `theme_example`, `theme_files`, `waterjet_tool`.\n- Pinning tests: the existing ribbon, status bar and shell tests in the ui lib pin the behaviour without change. Examples: `egui_app::tests::*` ribbon tests, `gate_route_tests`, `machine_mode_tests`, `pin_tests`, `ribbon_icon_tests`, `tests::structural`, `tests::page_layout`.\n- The release-lane pixel goldens do not match on this software adapter on main or on this head. This is not a change of this PR. The before/after renders above are the comparison.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The light lane: no heavy test reaches `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes`.\n- The example catalog suites: no post or toolpath change.\n- A run on a real GPU.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4393\n",
